## Context

Surfaced during ticket 0572 execution (PR #1042): after converting the
§exp2 F1 literal pairs to generated macros, the §exp2 cost medians
($0.73/$0.27) and row-count medians remain hand-typed in
`slides/manuscript/main.tex` — they are not F1 values and not derivable
from `tab_exp2_2x2.csv`, so they were out of 0572's scope. They are the
same defect class as ticket 0531 (manuscript numbers through generated
macros, `.claude/rules/writing.md`).

## Actions

1. Identify the committed artifact that owns these values (cost/row-count
   source per run); if none exists, extend the appropriate emitter to
   derive them from `measurements.jsonl` or the exp2 outputs.
2. Emit macros in the owning fragment (see `MANUSCRIPT_MACRO_FRAGMENTS`
   in `experiments/render.mk`), replace the inline literals, commit the
   regenerated fragments together with the consolidated
   `macros_manuscript.tex`.
3. Verify each macro value equals the literal it replaces; escalate any
   drift instead of silently accepting it.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] No hand-typed cost or row-count medians in §exp2; values flow from
  committed generated macro fragments
- [ ] `make check` passes
